---
// Two-layer cloud cap, same construction as the hero's SectionDivider (variant="clouds"):
// a back layer of large overlapping circles, a front layer of large overlapping circles plus
// a flat rect that turns their lower halves into a solid band (half-dome-on-a-band look).
//
// The hero's own circle data is tuned for a page-wide divider (~25 small circles spread over
// 1200 units) -- at card width that reads as a fine, busy texture rather than distinct cloud
// lumps. This is a purpose-built pattern instead: fewer, larger circles (6 back, 7 front)
// sized for a 368x74 cap. Positions were generated once with the same spacing rule as the
// original design spec (center-to-center spacing = 0.6 * (r + prevR), then spacing rescaled
// so the first circle's left edge lands exactly on x=0 and the last circle's right edge lands
// exactly on x=368) and hardcoded here, so every card renders the identical pattern with
// nothing clipped at the sides or top.
---

<div class="cloud-cap" aria-hidden="true">
  <svg class="cloud-cap__svg" viewBox="0 0 368 74" width="100%" height="74" preserveAspectRatio="none">
    <g fill="var(--midnight-lavender)"><circle cx="34" cy="48" r="34"/><circle cx="98.1" cy="42" r="40"/><circle cx="157.9" cy="51" r="29"/><circle cx="215.1" cy="43" r="37"/><circle cx="274" cy="50" r="31"/><circle cx="332" cy="41" r="36"/></g>
    <g fill="var(--midnight-navy)"><circle cx="26" cy="61" r="26"/><circle cx="79.9" cy="69" r="32"/><circle cx="131" cy="59" r="23"/><circle cx="180.2" cy="66" r="30"/><circle cx="231.4" cy="60" r="25"/><circle cx="285.2" cy="68" r="33"/><circle cx="341" cy="62" r="27"/><rect x="0" y="64" width="368" height="10"/></g>
  </svg>
</div>

<style>
  .cloud-cap {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    line-height: 0;
    margin-bottom: -1px;
  }

  .cloud-cap__svg {
    display: block;
    width: 100%;
    height: 74px;
  }
</style>
